<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĕōnĭdes</span></b> ,
		ae, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An instructor of Alexander the Great</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				14, 32, § 62</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 1,
				9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A teacher of the younger Cicero at Athens</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Att. 14, 16, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 16</span></i>, A; <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
				16, 21, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
